WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.580
We have already seen the characteristics of

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:12.200
images formed by plane mirrors.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.380
The image is of the same size as the object.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.980
And it's also at the same distance away from

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.160
the mirror as the object is.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.940
And the image follows left-right reversal.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.260
It means that the object's right is the image's left

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.740
and vice-versa.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.180
And lastly, the image formed by a plane mirror

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.020
is a virtual image.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.300
So what about the images formed by concave mirrors?

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:41.520
Do they have the same characteristics?

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.020
You all must have seen the reflection of your

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:47.960
face in a spoon. Spoon has two smooth surfaces

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:51.280
one curved inside and the other curved outside.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.760
However, it is not perfectly spherical.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.000
For ease of understanding, we can consider

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.520
the reflecting surface which is curved inwards

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.640
as a concave mirror.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.980
I will show you how the image appears,

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:08.540
but using an actual concave mirror and not a spoon.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.960
So let’s try and find out the properties

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.680
of an image formed by a CONCAVE MIRROR.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.640
I will show you two views of the mirror.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.040
The front view and the side view.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.960
The side view is just to show the different positions

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.320
where the object is kept, as it's difficult to

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.660
do that in the front view.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:32.820
Ok, so let ‘P’ be its pole, ‘C’ its centre of curvature,

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:37.860
this line is the principal axis and the ‘F’ is the principal focus.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.340
Also called focal point.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.960
Assume that initially, the object is kept close to the mirror.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.120
I will make a table on the right, with three columns

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.020
telling us the where the object is kept,

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.080
the size of the image formed and

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:54.760
the nature of the image, that is whether

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:57.640
the image is virtual or real.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:02.200
So initially the position of the object is between F and P.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.560
What is the size of the image?

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.940
We see the reflection in the concave mirror

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:09.660
and the image is BIGGER in size.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:12.220
We see that it's ENLARGED.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:15.110
The dimensions of the image are greater than the dimensions

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:16.400
of the object!

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.920
So we say that when the object is between

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.440
the principal focus and the pole, the image

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.740
formed is ENLARGED.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:27.740
Also is the image is upright or erect?

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:30.240
What about the nature of the image?

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:32.560
Is it real or virtual?

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.080
Yes, it's the virtual image!

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.940
It appears to be formed BEHIND the mirror!

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:40.720
Where is the location of the image?

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.800
It is a virtual image, so it does not have any location!

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:48.720
It only appears to be formed in a location behind the mirror.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:53.060
But we will find that location in our next video using ray diagrams.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.140
For now, let’s move this object away from

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:58.380
the mirror and see how the dimensions and

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:02.220
the nature of the image vary relative to the object.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.620
You will find that as I move this object away,

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.700
its image gets even bigger.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.780
And when the object is at the principal focus,

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:12.800
the image is HUGE.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:15.260
We say that when the object is at the principal

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:19.260
focus, the image is HIGHLY ENLARGED .

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.080
Is it a real or a virtual image?

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.120
It is a real image!

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:27.860
Since it's a real image, it's upside down!

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:31.500
Or we use the other word for it which is INVERTED.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.440
It is formed on the same side of the mirror

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.200
as the object is.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.940
And believe it or not, the image is actually

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.100
formed infinitely far away!

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.680
When I start moving this object away from

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.500
the focal point towards point C, the image

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:49.620
is still enlarged but the size is reducing.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.700
And what is the NATURE of this image?

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:58.220
Yes, here as well the image is upside down, it's a real image.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.640
When the object is at point C, the image

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.540
is still real and inverted but now the size

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:07.080
of the object and its image is same.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:10.140
Yes, at this point both the object and the

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.740
image are of the same size!

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.440
What next?

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.420
If I move this object beyond point C,

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.500
the image remains real and inverted, but now the

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.900
size of the image is actually smaller,

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:25.420
compared to the size of the object.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:28.740
So we say that the image is DIMINISHED.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.600
This is also a real image.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:35.020
As the objects keep moving beyond C, the size

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:37.240
of the image keeps on reducing.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.600
What if the object is placed at infinity?

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.420
Well if you remember that in our previous video,

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.660
we saw that the rays of light parallel to

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.660
each other as well as to the principal axis

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:51.180
will converge at the focal point.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:55.120
And in that example our object was the sun.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.700
Sun is at a very large distance away from

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:00.470
the earth and hence we consider the rays of light

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:02.220
from it reaching the surface of

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:05.240
the earth to be almost parallel.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:07.880
The image of the sun will be formed at the

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:09.500
principal focus.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.720
Similarly, if any object kept infinitely far

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.740
away from the mirror on the principal axis,

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.300
all the rays from it can be thought of as

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.760
travelling parallel to each other.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:25.440
After reflection, they will all converge at the focus.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.000
And the image of that infinitely far away

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.680
object will be formed at this point.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.660
Yes, this is a point sized image!

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:38.300
It is a highly diminished image and is also a real image.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.800
Take a moment and go through the properties

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.700
of images again.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.540
From this table you can see that the image

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:51.520
is virtual ONLY when the object is kept between

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.860
the focal point and the pole!

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:58.000
Otherwise the image formed is always a REAL image.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.000
In the next video we will find out the position

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.540
of these images using RAY diagrams.

